<p>Port Arthur fire damage claims are different from storm claims in almost every way. There is no question about whether something happened, and fire is a covered peril on nearly every property policy. The hard part is the size of the claim. A kitchen fire can push smoke through every room, firefighting water can soak floors on the other side of the house, and the family may be living somewhere else for months. Each of those is a separate piece of the claim with its own limits and documentation requirements. This page explains how fire claims are usually structured and where they tend to fall short.</p>

<h2>The Parts of a Fire Claim</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Claim component</th><th>Typical coverage</th><th>What you will need</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Structure</td><td>Dwelling (Coverage A) or commercial building coverage</td><td>Detailed repair or rebuild estimate</td></tr>
