<h2>Damage Beyond the Burned Area</h2>
<p>The visible burn is often a small share of the loss. Fire claims in Port Arthur homes frequently include:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Smoke and soot</strong> in rooms the fire never touched, inside wall cavities, attics, and HVAC ductwork. See our <a href="/services/smoke-damage-claims/">smoke damage claims</a> page for more on this.</li>
<li><strong>Heat damage</strong> to wiring, plumbing, windows, and finishes near the fire.</li>
<li><strong>Water and chemical damage</strong> from firefighting, which can soak subfloors in pier-and-beam homes and lead to mold in humid weather.</li>
<li><strong>Structural damage</strong> to framing, trusses, and roof decking that may not be obvious until demolition.</li>
<li><strong>Odor</strong> that lingers in porous materials such as insulation, carpet pad, and upholstered furniture.</li>
</ul>

