<h2>Rebuilding the Contents Inventory</h2>
<p>For many families, the contents inventory is the hardest part of a fire claim. Insurers usually want each item listed with a description, quantity, age, and replacement cost. Some practical ways to rebuild it:</p>
<ul>
<li>Walk through each room in your memory, wall by wall, closet by closet</li>
<li>Pull photos and videos from phones and social media that show rooms in the background</li>
<li>Download order histories from online retailers and review bank and credit card statements</li>
<li>Photograph damaged items before they are discarded, including labels and model numbers where possible</li>
</ul>
<p>Under replacement cost policies, contents are often paid at actual cash value first, with depreciation released after items are replaced. Track what you replace and keep receipts.</p>

