<h2>Rebuilding After a Fire in Port Arthur</h2>
<p>A significant fire usually means permits. The City of Port Arthur Building Inspections Division enforces the 2021 International Residential Code, International Building Code, International Plumbing Code, International Mechanical Code, and the 2020 National Electrical Code. Rewiring or replacing a burned section may require bringing that work up to current code. In Jefferson County, roof and structural repairs also need TDI windstorm inspection to keep TWIA eligibility. Whether your insurer pays for code upgrades depends on ordinance or law coverage. See our <a href="/local-building-codes/">local building codes</a> page.</p>

<h2>Where Fire Claims Fall Short</h2>
<ul>
<li>Cleaning allowed where replacement is needed, especially for smoke-saturated insulation and ductwork</li>
<li>Scope limited to the room of origin, with adjacent rooms left out</li>
<li>Contents values that rely on heavy depreciation or low-quality replacements</li>
<li>Living expense coverage cut off before the home is actually ready</li>
<li>Delays during the insurer’s cause-and-origin investigation</li>
</ul>
<p>If the claim has slowed or the payment is too low, see our pages on <a href="/services/delayed-insurance-claims/">delayed insurance claims</a> and <a href="/services/underpaid-insurance-claims/">underpaid insurance claims</a>. For disputes over the amount of loss, <a href="/services/insurance-appraisal/">appraisal</a> may be available under your policy.</p>

<h2>Total Loss or Repair?</h2>
<p>After a serious fire, one of the first big decisions is whether the building can be repaired or should be rebuilt. The insurer’s estimate may treat it as repairable while a contractor or engineer sees structural damage that makes rebuilding the more practical choice. Many Port Arthur homes are older pier-and-beam houses, and fire, heat, and firefighting water can all weaken framing and floor systems in ways that only show up during demolition. If the dwelling is a total loss, your policy limit, any extended replacement cost endorsement, debris removal, and ordinance or law coverage all become important. Ask for an engineer’s report when the condition of the structure is in question.</p>

<h2>How a Port Arthur Public Adjuster Helps After a Fire</h2>
<p>A public adjuster represents the policyholder, not the insurance company. After a fire, that may include documenting the structure with photos and 3D imaging such as Matterport, preparing a line-item Xactimate estimate, organizing the contents inventory, tracking living expenses, and communicating with the insurer’s adjuster and its consultants. For business owners, including those serving the refinery and port economy, we can help organize the building, inventory, and business income parts of a <a href="/services/commercial-property-claims/">commercial property claim</a>. Port Arthur Public Adjuster is a service of [[company]], TDI license #[[license]]. We cannot guarantee results, and fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement. If the insurer raises questions about the cause of the fire or requests an examination under oath, speak with a Texas attorney.</p>
